{
	"info": {
		"name": "Doriath Machine Secret-Store API Contract (secret-store-api v1)",
		"description": "Executable cross-repo contract for the doriath machine secret-store API (openspec change openconnector-secret-store-api, capability secret-store-api, apiVersion 1). This is the shared verification artifact the OpenConnector-side resolver — built in the openconnector repo with its own openspec change — is contract-tested against. Pin this collection alongside apiVersion.\n\nWHAT IT LOCKS: the discovery document shape; the token endpoint's grant/assertion validation and brute-force throttling; name-addressable retrieval (404 / single envelope / 409-with-candidates); the doriath-machine-secret-v1 envelope (format, encryption block with suiteId+certificateFingerprint+scheme, ciphertext-only — never plaintext); ETag/304 + updated_since rotation polling; client-encrypted write-back (POST/PUT, no delete route); and strict own-vault 404 scoping.\n\nZERO-KNOWLEDGE (ADR-003): every secret read returns CIPHERTEXT only; write-back payloads arrive pre-encrypted to the application's own certificate. The server never sees plaintext. Assertions verify the ciphertext block contains only the named base64 fields and that no plaintext-capable field appears.\n\nTWO RUN MODES:\n  (a) UNAUTHENTICATED CONTRACT (always runnable, no seed): the discovery document, the token-endpoint negative cases (unsupported grant, missing assertion -> 400 with throttle), and the bearer-required rejection of /api/v1/app/secrets. These run in every CI invocation.\n  (b) SEEDED MACHINE FLOW (token -> by-name -> envelope -> rotation -> write-back -> cross-vault 404): requires an approved application with a known private key. Provide seededAppId + seededPrivateKeyPem (PKCS#8 PEM) env vars; a pre-request script signs the RS256 JWT-bearer assertion. When the seed vars are absent the seeded requests skip their bodies honestly (pm.test.skip) — mirroring how the main doriath collection quarantines in-browser crypto-minting flows. The openconnector-side CI provides the seed and runs the full flow.\n\nAUTH MODEL: collection auth is noauth. Discovery + bearer-required tests target {{noAuthBase}} (127.0.0.1) so no NC session cookie leaks. Seeded requests carry an explicit Bearer header from the token exchange.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
		{ "key": "noAuthBase", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8080" },
		{ "key": "apiVersion", "value": "1" },
		{ "key": "seededAppId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "seededPrivateKeyPem", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "seededSecretName", "value": "zgw-api-token" },
		{ "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "fetchedEtag", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "createdSecretId", "value": "" }
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. Discovery (public, no auth)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "GET .well-known/doriath (200, self-describing)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/.well-known/doriath", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", ".well-known", "doriath"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK, JSON', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); pm.response.to.be.json; });",
									"const d = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('apiVersion matches the pinned contract', () => pm.expect(String(d.apiVersion)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('apiVersion')));",
									"pm.test('declares token endpoint + jwt-bearer grant', () => {",
									"  pm.expect(d.tokenEndpoint).to.be.a('string');",
									"  pm.expect(d.grantType).to.eql('urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer');",
									"});",
									"pm.test('declares assertion requirements', () => {",
									"  pm.expect(d.assertion.alg).to.eql('RS256');",
									"  pm.expect(d.assertion.maxLifetime).to.eql(300);",
									"});",
									"pm.test('declares list/byId/byName secret endpoints', () => {",
									"  pm.expect(d.secrets.list).to.be.a('string');",
									"  pm.expect(d.secrets.byId).to.include('{id}');",
									"  pm.expect(d.secrets.byName).to.include('by-name');",
									"});",
									"pm.test('declares the v1 envelope format', () => pm.expect(d.envelopeFormats).to.include('doriath-machine-secret-v1'));",
									"pm.test('advertises the lease policy additively (machine-secret-leases)', () => {",
									"  pm.expect(d.lease.supported).to.eql(true);",
									"  pm.expect(d.lease.defaultTtl).to.be.a('number');",
									"  pm.expect(d.lease.maxTtl).to.be.at.least(d.lease.defaultTtl);",
									"  pm.expect(d.lease.renewable).to.be.a('boolean');",
									"});",
									"pm.test('reveals no instance-private data', () => {",
									"  const flat = JSON.stringify(d);",
									"  ['privateKey','BEGIN CERTIFICATE','password'].forEach(n => pm.expect(flat).to.not.include(n));",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Token endpoint hardening (negative, no seed needed)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Unsupported grant type -> 400",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\"grant_type\":\"password\",\"assertion\":\"x\"}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/token", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "token"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('400 unsupported_grant_type', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('unsupported_grant_type');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Missing assertion -> 400",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\"grant_type\":\"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer\"}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/token", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "token"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('400 invalid_request', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('invalid_request');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Malformed assertion -> 401 (signature path)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\"grant_type\":\"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer\",\"assertion\":\"not.a.jwt\"}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/token", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "token"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('401 invalid_grant for a malformed assertion', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('invalid_grant');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "3. Bearer required on the secret surface (no auth)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "GET /app/secrets without a token -> 401",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('401 without a Bearer token', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "GET /app/secrets with a bogus token -> 401",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer deadbeefdeadbeef" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets"] }
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('401 with an invalid/expired token', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "4. Seeded machine flow (token -> by-name -> envelope -> rotation -> write-back -> scoping)",
			"description": "Requires seededAppId + seededPrivateKeyPem. Each request's pre-request script signs a fresh RS256 JWT-bearer assertion (aud='doriath', exp=iat+120, unique jti) and exchanges it for the access token, then runs the contract assertions. When the seed vars are absent the assertions are skipped honestly so the unauthenticated subset still passes in seedless CI.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Token exchange (happy path) -> opaque 5-min Bearer",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "prerequest",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"// Sign an RS256 JWT-bearer assertion with the seeded private key.",
									"// Requires the seed env vars; otherwise leave assertion empty and skip.",
									"const appId = pm.variables.get('seededAppId');",
									"const pem = pm.variables.get('seededPrivateKeyPem');",
									"if (!appId || !pem) { pm.variables.set('signedAssertion', ''); return; }",
									"const now = Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);",
									"const header = { alg: 'RS256', typ: 'JWT' };",
									"const payload = { iss: appId, aud: 'doriath', iat: now, exp: now + 120, jti: 'newman-' + now + '-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2) };",
									"// Signing uses node's crypto when run via newman (CryptoJS lacks RSA).",
									"try {",
									"  const crypto = require('crypto');",
									"  const b64u = (b) => Buffer.from(b).toString('base64').replace(/=+$/,'').replace(/\\+/g,'-').replace(/\\//g,'_');",
									"  const signingInput = b64u(JSON.stringify(header)) + '.' + b64u(JSON.stringify(payload));",
									"  const sig = crypto.sign('RSA-SHA256', Buffer.from(signingInput), pem);",
									"  const jws = signingInput + '.' + sig.toString('base64').replace(/=+$/,'').replace(/\\+/g,'-').replace(/\\//g,'_');",
									"  pm.variables.set('signedAssertion', jws);",
									"} catch (e) { pm.variables.set('signedAssertion', ''); console.log('assertion signing unavailable: ' + e.message); }"
								]
							}
						},
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.variables.get('seededAppId') && !!pm.variables.get('signedAssertion');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('token exchange returns an opaque 5-minute Bearer', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  const t = pm.response.json();",
									"  pm.expect(t.token_type).to.eql('Bearer');",
									"  pm.expect(t.expires_in).to.eql(300);",
									"  pm.expect(t.access_token).to.match(/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/);",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', t.access_token);",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\"grant_type\":\"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer\",\"assertion\":\"{{signedAssertion}}\"}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/token", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "token"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "by-name resolve -> doriath-machine-secret-v1 envelope (ciphertext only)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('envelope is self-describing and ciphertext-only', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  const e = pm.response.json();",
									"  pm.expect(e.format).to.eql('doriath-machine-secret-v1');",
									"  pm.expect(e.encryption.suiteId).to.be.a('string');",
									"  pm.expect(e.encryption.certificateFingerprint).to.match(/^sha256:/);",
									"  pm.expect(e.encryption.scheme).to.be.a('string');",
									"  pm.expect(Object.keys(e.ciphertext)).to.eql(['key','login','additionalFields']);",
									"  const flat = JSON.stringify(e);",
									"  pm.expect(flat).to.not.include('\"plaintext\"');",
									"  pm.expect(flat).to.not.include('\"value\"');",
									"  if (pm.response.headers.get('ETag')) pm.collectionVariables.set('fetchedEtag', pm.response.headers.get('ETag'));",
									"});",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('fetch grants a lease in headers (machine-secret-leases)', () => {",
									"  const leaseId = pm.response.headers.get('Doriath-Lease-Id');",
									"  const leaseExpires = pm.response.headers.get('Doriath-Lease-Expires');",
									"  pm.expect(leaseId).to.be.a('string').and.to.have.length.above(10);",
									"  pm.expect(Date.parse(leaseExpires)).to.be.above(Date.now());",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('leaseId', leaseId);",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets/by-name/{{seededSecretName}}", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets", "by-name", "{{seededSecretName}}"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "by-name unknown -> 404",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('unknown name returns 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets/by-name/this-name-does-not-exist-xyz", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets", "by-name", "this-name-does-not-exist-xyz"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "ETag 304 (rotation polling)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken') && !!pm.collectionVariables.get('fetchedEtag');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('matching If-None-Match returns 304', () => pm.response.to.have.status(304));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" },
							{ "key": "If-None-Match", "value": "{{fetchedEtag}}" }
						],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets/by-name/{{seededSecretName}}", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets", "by-name", "{{seededSecretName}}"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "updated_since filter (rotation polling)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('updated_since list returns the v1 envelope shape', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  const body = pm.response.json();",
									"  pm.expect(body.format).to.eql('doriath-machine-secret-v1');",
									"  pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets?updated_since=2000-01-01T00:00:00%2B00:00", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets"], "query": [{ "key": "updated_since", "value": "2000-01-01T00:00:00+00:00" }] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "write-back create -> 201 envelope",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('create returns 201 with the v1 envelope', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"  const e = pm.response.json();",
									"  pm.expect(e.format).to.eql('doriath-machine-secret-v1');",
									"  pm.collectionVariables.set('createdSecretId', e.secret.id);",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\"name\":\"newman-writeback\",\"key\":\"BASE64-CIPHERTEXT-PLACEHOLDER\"}" },
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "cross-vault id -> 404 (no existence oracle)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('a foreign/nonexistent id is 404, not 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/secrets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "secrets", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"] }
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "5. Machine leases (seeded; machine-secret-leases)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "list own leases -> contains the granted lease",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken') && !!pm.collectionVariables.get('leaseId');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('lease list contains the fetch-granted lease', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  const ids = pm.response.json().map(l => l.id);",
									"  pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('leaseId'));",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/leases", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "leases"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "renew lease -> expiry advances, count increments",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken') && !!pm.collectionVariables.get('leaseId');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('renewal succeeds within max lifetime', () => {",
									"  pm.expect([200, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
									"  if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
									"    const l = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(l.renewedCount).to.be.at.least(1);",
									"    pm.expect(Date.parse(l.expiresAt)).to.be.above(Date.now());",
									"  }",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/leases/{{leaseId}}/renew", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "leases", "{{leaseId}}", "renew"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "renew nonexistent lease -> 404 (no oracle)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('unknown lease id is 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/leases/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/renew", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "leases", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "renew"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "self-revoke lease -> revoked",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken') && !!pm.collectionVariables.get('leaseId');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('self-revocation marks the lease revoked', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('revoked');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{noAuthBase}}/apps/doriath/api/v1/app/leases/{{leaseId}}/revoke", "host": ["{{noAuthBase}}"], "path": ["apps", "doriath", "api", "v1", "app", "leases", "{{leaseId}}", "revoke"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "revoke-then-fetch (default policy) -> 200 with a NEW lease",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const seeded = !!pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken') && !!pm.collectionVariables.get('leaseId');",
									"(seeded ? pm.test : pm.test.skip)('default block-on-revoke=off re-grants on fetch', () => {",
									"  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"  const newLease = pm.response.headers.get('Doriath-Lease-Id');",
									"  pm.expect(newLease).to.be.a('string');",
									"  pm.expect(newLease).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('leaseId'));",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
